<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    HOP settings pane (Mode settings page) — the NET PROGRAMMING card.

    Round 4 (§AJ) gave the card TWO full-width SUB-TABS. Round 5 (§BE/§BG)
    rebuilds what is inside the programming tab:

      "Net programming"  LEFT, DEFAULT — the net picker, then EVERY FIELD ON
                         ITS OWN ROW (BE1): net ID, hop type, the TYPE-SWITCHED
                         value controls, and the actions. No Store, no blue
                         "Radio:" strip.
      "Net list"         RIGHT — ten READ-ONLY rows, nets 0-9, in the headed
                         cell style (CellHeading/CellValue + the CellWidth*
                         keys defined in App.xaml, round 4 K1).

    Round-5 constitution notes:
    - PER-FIELD WRITES (BG1). Each row commits its OWN radio command and then
      re-reads with `DIS n`. Entry rows commit on Return (ReturnCommand) or via
      their Set button — the same command either way.
    - TYPE-SWITCHED VALUES (BG2). The value section follows the net's CONFIRMED
      type: NB shows Center, WB shows Low/High, LIST shows the list UI, and an
      unreported type shows NO value controls. That is what enforces the wire's
      "HOPTYPE before HOPSET" ordering — there is no way to reach a value
      control except through a type the radio has already confirmed.
    - READ DISPLAYS (round-8 EA, superseding round-7 DB's value-backed
      placeholders): each field's REPORTED value renders in a blue inert
      ValueDisplay beside its entry (the RF-gain idiom, "—" until reported);
      the placeholders are plain format hints. The Text buffer is still
      always the operator's — typing starts clean, a report can never
      clobber typing, and an EMPTY field at commit still falls back to the
      reported value backing its display. The type segments still show the
      CONFIRMED type. A picker spin clears the entry text.
    - MHz (K6/BD2). Every frequency shown or typed here is MHz; the heading
      carries the unit and the cells and entries are bare numbers.
    - CLEAR NET (BG4) opens a warning on EVERY press and sends nothing until
      Proceed — HOPSET n DEL wipes the whole net record.
    - READ PATH (round 9, the unified two-tier doctrine): the EDITOR reads
      fresh per landing — a picker spin, a programming-tab landing, and the
      surface first becoming readable this session (initial sight, and the
      reconnect after a drop) each send `DIS n` for the PICKED net, plus
      `HOPLIST n` when it is confirmed LIST (BC4). The NET LIST tab is the
      lazy tier: its FIRST landing this session sends the whole-table `DIS`
      and re-arms the hoplist once-set; nothing else sends a `DIS`-all.
      The pane's Refresh button is DELETED — every landing re-reads.

    ROUND 11 (§7, owner ruling R11 / scope amendment X9) adds a SECOND CARD
    below the net-programming one: "Exclusion bands", the WB exclusion table in
    the LIST-editor idiom. It is its own card because the wire's `EXC` names no
    net — the table is global, not a property of the picked net — and it rides
    the same editors-read-fresh tier the net editor uses. §7 also closes the
    LIST add box's delimiter to SPACE and re-words the Clear-net popup (the
    wipe resets the type to WB).

    ROUND 14 B (owner ruling R2) adds a THIRD CARD: the ANTENNA COUPLER row,
    copied from the SSB settings pane and reading the same mirror.
    ROUND 15 H-1 (owner) puts it FIRST and deletes its advisory caption, so the
    pane reads: ANTENNA COUPLER - Net programming - Exclusion bands - (outside
    the gate) the radio clock. It leads because it is the setting to check
    BEFORE programming a net, not a footnote below the editor that depends on
    it.

    Binding: the ContentView root inherits the hosting page's ModeViewModel so
    ModeSettingsPage's IsVisible="{Binding IsHopActive}" keeps resolving; only
    the inner Body rebinds to HopSettingsViewModel (the AleSettingsPaneView
    pattern).
-->
<ContentView xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:Falcon.App.Core.ViewModels;assembly=Falcon.App.Core"
             xmlns:parts="clr-namespace:Falcon.App.Views.SettingsParts"
             xmlns:behaviors="clr-namespace:Falcon.App.Behaviors"
             x:Class="Falcon.App.Views.SettingsParts.HopSettingsPaneView">

    <ContentView.Resources>
        <!-- F4 (plan-clone-field-round2.md, decision A-2) — THE CRASH FIX.
             The coupler row copied in round 14 B (3d430d0) came with a
             `{StaticResource ChoiceButton}` binding, but the template it names
             lives only in SsbSettingsPaneView's OWN resources. A ContentView
             resolves a StaticResource at InitializeComponent time against its
             own dictionary and the application's — never a SIBLING view's — so
             ModeSettingsPage, which constructs all three panes eagerly, died
             with `XamlParseException: Position 477:52. StaticResource not found
             for key ChoiceButton` on every entry, in all three modes (crash
             buffer, adb logcat -b crash, 2026-08-21; three identical frames).

             The fix is the r14-b idiom, not a shared dictionary: this pane owns
             its own copy under its own key. The key is DELIBERATELY DISTINCT
             (`HopChoiceButton`) so that a future copy-paste of a row out of
             this file carries a name that says where it came from, and so the
             structural guard (XamlResourceGuardTests) has a named target to
             pin rather than a name that happens to exist in three files.

             VERBATIM copy of SsbSettingsPaneView.xaml's `ChoiceButton`. If that
             one changes, this one is a separate decision — which is exactly
             what A-2 chose over a shared dictionary. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="HopChoiceButton" x:DataType="vm:ChoiceItem">
            <Button Text="{Binding Value}" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                    WidthRequest="{StaticResource SegmentWidth}"
                    Command="{Binding SelectCommand}"
                    SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding Value}">
                <Button.Triggers>
                    <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsActive}" Value="True">
                        <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                        <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                    </DataTrigger>
                </Button.Triggers>
            </Button>
        </DataTemplate>
    </ContentView.Resources>

    <ScrollView x:Name="Body" x:DataType="vm:HopSettingsViewModel">
        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="{OnIdiom Default=12, Phone=8}">

            <!-- ============ Antenna coupler (round 14 B, R2) =================
                 The owner's ask, verbatim: "copy the SSB settings screen's
                 control buttons". This IS that row — SsbSettingsPaneView.xaml's
                 "Internal coupler" grid, cell for cell — reading and writing
                 the SAME Core mirror. Two placements of one confirmed value:
                 press Bypass here and the SSB pane's row lights Bypass too,
                 with no synchronisation code anywhere, because there is only
                 ever one state.

                 WHY IT IS HERE. Wide-band and list nets do not generate
                 while the internal coupler is enabled — manual Table 1-5, and
                 BENCH-PROVEN by P-1 run B (the same WB tuple answered
                 `WB_Invalid` with the coupler enabled and generated
                 `Hopnum 0101` with it bypassed). ROUND 15 H-1 (owner) moves it
                 to the TOP of the pane: it is the setting to check before
                 programming a net, not a footnote below the editor that
                 depends on it. Round 14 B had it between the net editor and
                 the exclusion table.

                 ITS ADVISORY CAPTION IS DELETED (H-1). The restriction is
                 documented in docs/ui.md; a standing paragraph on a one-row
                 card was furniture, and the card now leads the pane, where a
                 heading and a row read faster than a heading, a row and a
                 warning.

                 ITS OWN CARD, like the exclusion table beside it, for the same
                 reason: the coupler is RADIO state, not a property of the
                 picked net, so it does not belong inside the per-net editor.

                 The buttons ALWAYS SEND — no re-click guard — and only the
                 radio's echo (`INTCoupler Bypassed` / `INTCoupler Enabled`,
                 P-1 captured) lights one. That is the provisional-trio contract
                 inherited whole from the copied row (docs/ui.md). -->
            <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}">
                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10">
                    <Label Text="Antenna coupler" Style="{StaticResource CardHeading}" />

                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsEnabled="{Binding AreControlsEnabled}">
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6">
                            <Label Text="Internal coupler" VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" />
                            <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Spacing="6" HorizontalOptions="End"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding InternalCouplerChoices}"
                                                   BindableLayout.ItemTemplate="{StaticResource HopChoiceButton}" />
                        </Grid>
                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                </VerticalStackLayout>
            </Border>

            <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}">
                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10">

                    <Label Text="Net programming" Style="{StaticResource CardHeading}" />

                    <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}" Text="{Binding DisabledReason}"
                           IsVisible="{Binding HasDisabledReason}" />

                    <!-- Sub-tab strip — CARD-level, so INSIDE the card (T3),
                         full width, under the heading. Pure view state:
                         switching sends nothing. Programming is the DEFAULT
                         (IsListTabOpen starts false) and sits LEFT. The strip
                         stays usable outside the gate — it switches a view, it
                         does not touch the radio. -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                        <Button Text="Net programming" Style="{StaticResource Segment}" HorizontalOptions="Fill"
                                Command="{Binding OpenProgrammingTabCommand}"
                                SemanticProperties.Description="Net programming tab (picker and per-field editors)">
                            <Button.Triggers>
                                <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsListTabOpen}" Value="False">
                                    <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                                    <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                                </DataTrigger>
                            </Button.Triggers>
                        </Button>
                        <Button Grid.Column="1" Text="Net list" Style="{StaticResource Segment}" HorizontalOptions="Fill"
                                Command="{Binding OpenListTabCommand}"
                                SemanticProperties.Description="Net list tab (all ten nets, read-only)">
                            <Button.Triggers>
                                <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsListTabOpen}" Value="True">
                                    <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                                    <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                                </DataTrigger>
                            </Button.Triggers>
                        </Button>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- Everything the gate greys: both tab bodies. Outside
                         Ready + confirmed HOP the card is silently inert. -->
                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsEnabled="{Binding AreControlsEnabled}">

                        <!-- ========= Net programming tab (BE1: one row each) ========= -->
                        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="True">
                            <VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>
                                <DataTrigger TargetType="VerticalStackLayout" Binding="{Binding IsListTabOpen}" Value="True">
                                    <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
                                </DataTrigger>
                            </VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>

                            <!-- ROW 1 — the net picker. APP-SIDE view state
                                 (which net every row below addresses). ROUND 9:
                                 a spin is an EDITOR LANDING and READS the net
                                 it lands on (DIS n, plus HOPLIST n for a
                                 confirmed LIST net) — the round-5 "the picker
                                 sends nothing" ruling is reversed here. It is
                                 also a populate gesture, so the entries CLEAR
                                 and the read displays show the landed net's
                                 reported values (round-7 DB / round-8 EA).
                                 Round 6 (CC): the explanatory caption beside
                                 the picker is GONE (owner) — the picker stands
                                 alone. -->
                            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="0" HorizontalOptions="Start">
                                <Button Text="▲" FontSize="10" Padding="0"
                                        WidthRequest="44" HeightRequest="44"
                                        Command="{Binding NetUpCommand}"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Show the next net — re-reads it from the radio (DIS n)" />
                                <!-- Round 10 §3: the spinner digit is a NAMED
                                     style now (SpinnerDigit) — the width stays
                                     at the use site, as the key's note says. -->
                                <Label Text="{Binding PickedNetText}"
                                       Style="{StaticResource SpinnerDigit}"
                                       WidthRequest="44" />
                                <Button Text="▼" FontSize="10" Padding="0"
                                        WidthRequest="44" HeightRequest="44"
                                        Command="{Binding NetDownCommand}"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Show the previous net — re-reads it from the radio (DIS n)" />
                            </VerticalStackLayout>

                            <!-- ROW 2 — net ID (NETID n, then DIS n). Round 8
                                 (EA, owner): the blue ValueDisplay left of the
                                 entry is the RF-gain idiom — the CONFIRMED
                                 reported value, "—" until reported, K-fixed
                                 width (8 digits / the X-form). The placeholder
                                 is a plain hint again. -->
                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6">
                                <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                       Text="Net ID" WidthRequest="86" />
                                <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplay}"
                                        WidthRequest="{StaticResource ValueWidthXWide}"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Net ID reported value">
                                    <Label Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplayText}"
                                           Text="{Binding NetIdDisplayText}" />
                                </Border>
                                <Entry Grid.Column="2" Keyboard="Numeric" MaxLength="8"
                                       Placeholder="8 digits"
                                       Text="{Binding NetIdInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       ReturnCommand="{Binding CommitNetIdCommand}"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Net ID entry — empty re-sends the reported ID" />
                                <Button Grid.Column="3" Text="Set" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                        WidthRequest="{StaticResource SegmentWidth}"
                                        Command="{Binding CommitNetIdCommand}"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Write this net ID to the radio" />
                            </Grid>

                            <!-- ROW 3 — hop type (HOPTYPE n, then DIS n).
                                 ROUND 13 (plan/plan-round13.md §4 A1):
                                 item 9 (owner 2026-08-19) RIGHT-JUSTIFIES the
                                 three segments — the residual star column is
                                 col 1, ahead of them, and nothing sits in it;
                                 item 14 (ruling 2026-08-20) moves the
                                 highlight from the CONFIRMED type to the
                                 REPORTED one, so a type press lights on the
                                 radio's echo even before a net ID lands. The
                                 gates did NOT move: the value sections below
                                 stay bound to Is*Confirmed and the re-click
                                 guard still reads the confirmed type, so a lit
                                 segment on a reported-but-unconfirmed net
                                 still sends (a harmless duplicate). -->
                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6">
                                <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                       Text="Type" WidthRequest="86" />
                                <Button Grid.Column="2" Text="NB" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                        WidthRequest="{StaticResource SegmentWidth}"
                                        Command="{Binding SetTypeCommand}" CommandParameter="NB"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Set narrowband">
                                    <Button.Triggers>
                                        <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsNarrowbandReported}" Value="True">
                                            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                                            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                                        </DataTrigger>
                                    </Button.Triggers>
                                </Button>
                                <Button Grid.Column="3" Text="WB" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                        WidthRequest="{StaticResource SegmentWidth}"
                                        Command="{Binding SetTypeCommand}" CommandParameter="WB"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Set wideband">
                                    <Button.Triggers>
                                        <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsWidebandReported}" Value="True">
                                            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                                            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                                        </DataTrigger>
                                    </Button.Triggers>
                                </Button>
                                <Button Grid.Column="4" Text="LIST" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                        WidthRequest="{StaticResource SegmentWidth}"
                                        Command="{Binding SetTypeCommand}" CommandParameter="LIST"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Set hop list">
                                    <Button.Triggers>
                                        <DataTrigger TargetType="Button" Binding="{Binding IsListReported}" Value="True">
                                            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AccentColor}" />
                                            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource OnAccentColor}" />
                                        </DataTrigger>
                                    </Button.Triggers>
                                </Button>
                            </Grid>

                            <!-- ROW 4a is GONE (round 6, CC — owner ruling):
                                 with no confirmed type the value controls are
                                 simply ABSENT (BG2); no caption says so. -->


                            <!-- ROW 4b — NB: one center (HOPSET n c, then DIS n).
                                 EA: blue read display beside the entry; hint
                                 placeholder. -->
                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6"
                                  IsVisible="{Binding IsNarrowbandConfirmed}">
                                <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                       Text="Center (MHz)" WidthRequest="86" />
                                <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplay}"
                                        WidthRequest="{StaticResource ValueWidthWide}"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Center frequency reported value, MHz">
                                    <Label Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplayText}"
                                           Text="{Binding CenterDisplayText}" />
                                </Border>
                                <Entry Grid.Column="2" Keyboard="Numeric"
                                       Placeholder="MHz, e.g. 11.565"
                                       Text="{Binding CenterInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                       ReturnCommand="{Binding CommitCenterCommand}"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Narrowband center frequency in MHz — empty re-sends the reported center" />
                                <Button Grid.Column="3" Text="Set" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                        WidthRequest="{StaticResource SegmentWidth}"
                                        Command="{Binding CommitCenterCommand}"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Write the center frequency to the radio" />
                            </Grid>

                            <!-- ROW 4c — WB: the two band edges. One command
                                 carries both (HOPSET n low high), and since
                                 round 6 (CB, owner) ONE Set below the pair
                                 sends it — the per-row duplicates are gone.
                                 Return on either entry still commits. -->
                            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="{Binding IsWidebandConfirmed}">
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                                    <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                           Text="Low (MHz)" WidthRequest="86" />
                                    <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplay}"
                                            WidthRequest="{StaticResource ValueWidthWide}"
                                            SemanticProperties.Description="Low edge reported value, MHz">
                                        <Label Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplayText}"
                                               Text="{Binding LowDisplayText}" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Entry Grid.Column="2" Keyboard="Numeric"
                                           Placeholder="MHz, e.g. 2.000"
                                           Text="{Binding LowInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                           ReturnCommand="{Binding CommitBandEdgesCommand}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Wideband low edge in MHz — empty sends the reported edge" />
                                </Grid>
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="6">
                                    <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                           Text="High (MHz)" WidthRequest="86" />
                                    <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplay}"
                                            WidthRequest="{StaticResource ValueWidthWide}"
                                            SemanticProperties.Description="High edge reported value, MHz">
                                        <Label Style="{StaticResource ValueDisplayText}"
                                               Text="{Binding HighDisplayText}" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Entry Grid.Column="2" Keyboard="Numeric"
                                           Placeholder="MHz, e.g. 8.000"
                                           Text="{Binding HighInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                           ReturnCommand="{Binding CommitBandEdgesCommand}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="Wideband high edge in MHz — empty sends the reported edge" />
                                </Grid>
                                <Button Text="Set" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                        WidthRequest="{StaticResource SegmentWidth}"
                                        HorizontalOptions="End"
                                        Command="{Binding CommitBandEdgesCommand}"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Write both band edges to the radio" />
                            </VerticalStackLayout>

                            <!-- ROW 4d — LIST: the stored frequencies as
                                 removable rows (BG3), then one add box. The
                                 rows come from the BC4 `HOPLIST n` read; ADD is
                                 APPEND on the wire, which is fine now that
                                 every entry is visible and removable. -->
                            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="{Binding IsListConfirmed}">
                                <!-- Round 10 §3: this is a SECTION HEAD, not a
                                     column heading — SubHeading. The table's
                                     own header row is below it. -->
                                <Label Text="Frequencies (MHz)" Style="{StaticResource SubHeading}" />

                                <!-- Round 10 §3: the list editor is a TABLE, so
                                     it gets a header row. The Remove column is
                                     deliberately UNHEADED — a heading over a
                                     column of buttons names nothing. -->
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6">
                                    <Label Text="Freq" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                           WidthRequest="{StaticResource CellWidthValue}" />
                                </Grid>

                                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="6"
                                                     BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding ListRows}">
                                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:HopFrequencyRow">
                                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6">
                                                <Label Text="{Binding MhzText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource CellWidthValue}"
                                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Stored hop frequency" />
                                                <Button Grid.Column="2" Text="Remove" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                                        Command="{Binding Remove}"
                                                        CommandParameter="{Binding FrequencyKHz}"
                                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Remove this frequency from the net's hop list" />
                                            </Grid>
                                        </DataTemplate>
                                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                </VerticalStackLayout>
                                <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding HasNoListFrequencies}"
                                       Text="No frequencies reported for this net yet." />
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6">
                                    <!-- The label text stays exactly "Add" — the
                                         type-section guard LOCATES the LIST
                                         section by it (invariant 6). -->
                                    <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                           Text="Add" WidthRequest="86" />
                                    <!-- Round 7 (DC, owner): a HINT, not
                                         something that reads like values. -->
                                    <!-- ROUND 11 §7: the placeholder NAMES the
                                         delimiter, because the delimiter is now
                                         SPACE and nothing else — a comma is a
                                         decimal comma to most of the world, and
                                         splitting on it sent two frequencies
                                         where the operator typed one. -->
                                    <Entry Grid.Column="1"
                                           Placeholder="{x:Static vm:HopSettingsViewModel.ListAddPlaceholder}"
                                           Text="{Binding ListAddInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                           ReturnCommand="{Binding AddListFrequenciesCommand}"
                                           SemanticProperties.Description="One or more frequencies in MHz, space separated" >
                                        <Entry.Behaviors>
                                            <behaviors:SelectAllOnFocusBehavior />
                                        </Entry.Behaviors>
                                    </Entry>
                                    <Button Grid.Column="2" Text="Add" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                            Command="{Binding AddListFrequenciesCommand}"
                                            SemanticProperties.Description="Add these frequencies to the net's hop list" />
                                </Grid>
                            </VerticalStackLayout>

                            <!-- ROW 5 — actions. Clear net is destructive, so it
                                 asks on EVERY press. ROUND 10 §5: the inline
                                 Proceed/Cancel strip and its warning box are
                                 DELETED — the question is a two-button POPUP
                                 (IConfirmationPrompt; the VM never touches MAUI
                                 UI) that NAMES the net it captured at press, so
                                 moving the picker while it is open cannot
                                 redirect the wipe. The strip's markup pins moved
                                 with it, into the VM's lifecycle tests. -->
                            <Button Text="Clear net" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                    HorizontalOptions="Start"
                                    Command="{Binding RequestNetWipeCommand}"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="Wipe this net's whole record on the radio" />

                            <Label Style="{StaticResource ErrorCaption}" Text="{Binding InputError}"
                                   IsVisible="{Binding HasInputError}" />
                        </VerticalStackLayout>

                        <!-- ================== Net list tab ================== -->
                        <!-- Ten READ-ONLY rows in the headed-cell style: the
                             column headings are carried ONCE at the top of the
                             table, and every row uses the same CellValue style
                             and CellWidth* keys as the Operate pane's "Current
                             net" row, so the columns line up and the widths
                             stay tunable in one place (K1). The value column is
                             headed "Frequencies (MHz)" in BOTH panes (BD1) and
                             its cells come from the shared HopNetDisplay
                             vocabulary, so one mirror state cannot render two
                             ways. No controls anywhere in this tab. -->
                        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="6" IsVisible="False">
                            <VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>
                                <DataTrigger TargetType="VerticalStackLayout" Binding="{Binding IsListTabOpen}" Value="True">
                                    <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="True" />
                                </DataTrigger>
                            </VerticalStackLayout.Triggers>

                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                <Label Text="Net" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource CellWidthNet}" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="ID" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource CellWidthId}" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="Type" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource CellWidthType}" />
                                <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="Frequencies (MHz)" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                       WidthRequest="{StaticResource CellWidthValue}" />
                            </Grid>

                            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="6"
                                                 BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding Rows}">
                                <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:HopNetListRow">
                                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                            <Label Text="{Binding NumberText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                                   WidthRequest="{StaticResource CellWidthNet}"
                                                   SemanticProperties.Description="Net number" />
                                            <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding NetIdText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                                   WidthRequest="{StaticResource CellWidthId}"
                                                   SemanticProperties.Description="Reported net ID" />
                                            <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding TypeText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                                   WidthRequest="{StaticResource CellWidthType}"
                                                   SemanticProperties.Description="Reported hop type" />
                                            <Label Grid.Column="3" Text="{Binding ValueText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                                   WidthRequest="{StaticResource CellWidthValue}"
                                                   SemanticProperties.Description="Reported frequencies in MHz" />
                                        </Grid>
                                    </DataTemplate>
                                </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                            </VerticalStackLayout>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                </VerticalStackLayout>
            </Border>

            <!-- ============ Exclusion bands (round 11 §7, R11/X9) ============
                 A NEW section, and its OWN card: the wire's `EXC` names no net,
                 so this table is GLOBAL and does not belong inside the
                 per-net editor above.

                 The LIST-editor idiom, verbatim from the hop-frequency editor
                 beside it: a header row, read-only value cells with a per-row
                 Remove, then one add row. Per-row Remove is UNCONFIRMED — the
                 round-10 §5 popup matrix covers whole-record destruction
                 (Clear net / Delete address / Erase) and explicitly does NOT
                 extend to per-row Removes.

                 THREE DISPLAY STATES, from the Core mirror (invariant 6):
                 UNREAD renders exactly ONE hyphen row (no Remove beside it);
                 READ-EMPTY renders the caption; rows otherwise. The two are
                 distinguishable only because the read is sentinel-bracketed —
                 an empty exclusion table answers NOTHING AT ALL.

                 MHz in, MHz out — but the SET command takes 8-DIGIT Hz, and
                 the conversion asserts exactly eight digits before the send
                 (the 5-digit rule's sibling: the radio silently IGNORES a
                 wrongly-shaped frequency, so a short value is misread, not
                 refused).

                 WIRE SHAPES PROVISIONAL (plan §14) except the captured
                 single-band echo: the multi-band listing layout, the DEL echo
                 variants and the band bounds are patterned, not observed.

                 ROW BUDGET (literal columns, the round-11 §4 idiom):
                 56 + 76 + 76 + 3x8 = 232 dp of fixed cells, plus the
                 action-class Remove (~84) = 316 <= 336 dp of phone card
                 content. "29.995" is six Consolas-18 glyphs (~60 dp) <= 76. -->
            <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}">
                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10">
                    <Label Text="Exclusion bands" Style="{StaticResource CardHeading}" />

                    <!-- The two wire facts no control on screen shows. -->
                    <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                           Text="{x:Static vm:HopSettingsViewModel.ExcludeCaption}" />

                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsEnabled="{Binding AreControlsEnabled}">

                        <!-- Header row. The Remove column is deliberately
                             UNHEADED — a heading over a column of buttons names
                             nothing (§3's table rule, as applied to the
                             hop-frequency editor above). -->
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                            <Label Text="Band" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                   WidthRequest="56" />
                            <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="Low (MHz)" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                   WidthRequest="76" />
                            <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="High (MHz)" Style="{StaticResource CellHeading}"
                                   WidthRequest="76" />
                        </Grid>

                        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="6"
                                             BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding ExcludeDisplayRows}">
                            <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:HopExcludeRow">
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                        <Label Text="{Binding BandText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                               WidthRequest="56"
                                               SemanticProperties.Description="Exclusion band slot" />
                                        <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding LowText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                               WidthRequest="76"
                                               SemanticProperties.Description="Excluded band low edge in MHz" />
                                        <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding HighText}" Style="{StaticResource CellValue}"
                                               WidthRequest="76"
                                               SemanticProperties.Description="Excluded band high edge in MHz" />
                                        <!-- Hidden on the UNREAD placeholder: a
                                             Remove beside a hyphen would offer
                                             to delete the marker. -->
                                        <Button Grid.Column="3" Text="Remove" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                                HorizontalOptions="End"
                                                IsVisible="{Binding CanRemove}"
                                                Command="{Binding RemoveBand}"
                                                CommandParameter="{Binding BandText}"
                                                SemanticProperties.Description="Remove this exclusion band from the radio" />
                                    </Grid>
                                </DataTemplate>
                            </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>

                        <!-- State 2 of three: the radio's ANSWERED-and-empty
                             table. The unread state is the hyphen ROW above. -->
                        <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding HasNoExcludeBands}"
                               Text="{x:Static vm:HopSettingsViewModel.NoExcludeBandsCaption}" />

                        <!-- Add row → the NEXT FREE band slot 0-9. -->
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="6">
                            <!-- "Add band", NOT "Add": the type-section guard
                                 LOCATES the net editor's LIST section by a
                                 Label whose Text is exactly "Add" (invariant 6),
                                 and a second one would make that anchor
                                 ambiguous. -->
                            <Label VerticalOptions="Center" Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                                   Text="Add band" WidthRequest="56" />
                            <Entry Grid.Column="1" Keyboard="Numeric"
                                   Placeholder="Low MHz"
                                   Text="{Binding ExcludeLowInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                   ReturnCommand="{Binding AddExcludeBandCommand}"
                                   SemanticProperties.Description="Exclusion band low edge in MHz" />
                            <Entry Grid.Column="2" Keyboard="Numeric"
                                   Placeholder="High MHz"
                                   Text="{Binding ExcludeHighInput, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                   ReturnCommand="{Binding AddExcludeBandCommand}"
                                   SemanticProperties.Description="Exclusion band high edge in MHz" />
                            <Button Grid.Column="3" Text="Add" Style="{StaticResource Segment}"
                                    Command="{Binding AddExcludeBandCommand}"
                                    SemanticProperties.Description="Add this exclusion band to the radio's next free band slot" />
                        </Grid>

                        <!-- Why Add is unavailable: all ten slots used, or the
                             table has not been read yet (adding into an unknown
                             table would have to GUESS a free slot). -->
                        <Label Style="{StaticResource Caption}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding HasAddExcludeBandDisabledReason}"
                               Text="{Binding AddExcludeBandDisabledReason}" />

                        <Label Style="{StaticResource ErrorCaption}" Text="{Binding ExcludeError}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding HasExcludeError}" />
                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                </VerticalStackLayout>
            </Border>

            <!-- The shared radio clock (round-4 AD/K2): the same
                 DeviceClockView as Radio settings, over the same VM state,
                 OUTSIDE the pane's grey gate — the clock is global. -->
            <parts:DeviceClockView />

            <!-- ROUND 9: the pane-bottom Refresh button is DELETED (the BG6
                 bottom-of-pane instance retires with it). Under the unified
                 read doctrine an EDITOR landing re-reads its target every
                 time — a picker spin and a programming-tab landing each send
                 DIS n (+ HOPLIST n for a confirmed LIST net) — so a manual
                 "read the radio" button here answered a question the picker
                 already answers. Refresh buttons now exist ONLY on
                 expensive-bulk list surfaces (the SSB channel list tab's
                 DI ×100), which keeps its own. -->

        </VerticalStackLayout>
    </ScrollView>
</ContentView>
